Okey dokey.

Initially, I wanted to try for a atheist wishless necromancer.

I started with a ring of polycontrol, which is a HUGE boon for a
doppelganger.

I used my pickaxe as a weapon until I got a mattock, which I used until
I completed the quest.

Minetown had two magic lamps and a gauntlets of power.

The max-hp drain from a hp-induced de-polymorph was very damaging,
kicking me back to as low as 54 max hp at level 12.  Alchemy eventually
fixed me up, bringing me to a high of 388 max hp.  Death ended up
kicking me back to 294, though.

It took me a very long time to get magic resistance and reflection.
Shortly before that, a damned brownie on the Nightmare level (lawful
quest) managed to vaporize my GoP.

I eventually used !poGL upgrading to make a few useful items like a
cloak of MR, [GoDex, [HoBril, and 2 saddles, one after my ride was
disintegrated out from under me.

Only found one magic marker.

A stupid moat accident blanked a bunch of enchant armor and identify
scrolls I had paid a fortune for from the Black Market.

Later, I used thrown poisoned daggers to kill One Eye'd Sam and steal
his armor.

In the late game, I had a pet level 45 purple worm named BigGulp. I
kept a wand of undead turning to bring him back a few times, but On
Astral one of my other pets managed to eat his corpse before I could
zap :(

On the way up with the Amulet, I was getting stoned by an unlucky
cockatrice hiss, while I was burdened, very satiated, and without a
lizard corpse. One zap from my wand of polymorph and I was a gargoyle.

Taming Death was done by the following procedure:
1) Engrave Elbereth with /WoFire
2) Put on rings of free action and levitation.
3) Wield a potion of paralysis
4) quaff potion of invulnerability
5) Hit death with potion of paralysis.
6) Polymorph into a green slime
7) Bite Death until it transforms
8) #youpoly back into a human.
9) Cast Charm Monster.
10) Remove ring of levitation
11) Pick up armor and get dressed.

There was a wand store on level 35 that offered charging.  I used it to
charge up most of my useful wands before I made my final ascent.

I never found a spellbook of +FoD, but I did ok with the three wands of
death I found.

After BigGulp swallowed my friendly High Priest, I came awfully close
to losing  atheist conduct by dropping a scroll of scare monster on the
altar. Fortunately, I remembered just in time.

Happy hacking.

